From d96dc5bd3aabb0f68a9a09d66b5f79cb0a9a3e98 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ajensenwaud <ajensenwaud@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 04:39:30 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 22/29] inkling2: Mini's draft pass takes every stream through
 each launch once

The pass already ran the drafter's projections over every block's rows, but
the attention, q/k prep, Markov context, recurrence and picks still ran a
stream at a time, and so did each stream's absorb. At 8 streams that cost as
much as a whole 8-row forward. Mini now runs one launch a step for all
streams (dspark_many.cuh, a stream table uploaded once a pass), absorbs
every stream's kept rows together, and drafts at every width by default.
Each row's arithmetic is the per-stream kernels', so the drafts are the
same bits. Small keeps its released pass. TF_INKLING2_DRAFT_BATCH=0 puts
Mini back on the per-stream pass; tf-inkling2-engine multi checks drafted
== plain at 1/2/4/8 streams and the two passes against each other.
